## 2. Strongly-Typed Asset Contracts

Centralizing asset references in strongly-typed code modules prevents runtime string misspellings and missing resource crashes.

<Tabs>
  <TabItem label="Android (Compose)">

```kotlin
// File: core/designsystem/theme/BrandIcons.kt
package com.enterprise.mobile.core.designsystem.theme

import androidx.annotation.DrawableRes
import androidx.compose.ui.graphics.vector.ImageVector

object BrandIcons {
    // Vector Drawable Resource Enums
    val AppLogo: Int = R.drawable.ic_brand_logo
    val UserAvatarPlaceholder: Int = R.drawable.ic_avatar_placeholder
    val SecurityShield: Int = R.drawable.ic_security_shield
    
    // System Status Icons
    val CheckmarkCircle: Int = R.drawable.ic_check_circle
    val WarningTriangle: Int = R.drawable.ic_warning_triangle
}
```

